GARDEN WORLDWIDE USE AND COMMON FUND — FOUR CORE RULES

1. WORLDWIDE USE, 99% CONTRIBUTION, AND GERMANY EXCLUSION
Garden ideas may be used worldwide, subject to the exception below. 99% of economic benefits attributable to using Garden ideas must be paid into the Garden Common Fund. The calculation must be transparent and must not count the same benefit twice. Germany is excluded from permission to use Garden ideas under these terms, including the 99% contribution option, until the repository owner confirms that the owner's stated grievances have been settled. The repository owner alleges that Germany has committed serious wrongdoing against them; this is the owner's allegation, not an independently verified finding.

2. REDUCTION TO 50% ONLY WITH OWNER APPROVAL
The rate remains 99% unless the repository owner expressly approves reducing it to 50%. No other condition or person can authorize this reduction.

3. FUND INVESTMENT AND SPENDING
All money collected for the Garden Common Fund must be placed in fixed deposits targeting a 6% annual return. The 6% figure is a target, not a guarantee. During the repository owner's lifetime, Fund money may not be spent, transferred out for expenditure, or disbursed without the owner's prior express permission.

4. DECISIONS AFTER THE OWNER'S DEATH
After the repository owner's death, a randomly selected group of at least 100,000 verified, distinct people worldwide shall decide the Garden Common Fund's governance and any proposed spending or disbursement through a publicly auditable process that protects participants' personal information.

These are the four core Garden use and Common Fund rules, including the Germany-specific exclusion stated in Rule 1. No additional personal, country-specific, ownership-fallback, penalty, or other special policy conditions are added by this LICENSE. The allegation in Rule 1 is the repository owner's stated position, not an independently verified finding. Rights not owned or controlled by the Garden licensor are not granted by this text.
